    "deep": "\n<div class=\"deep sheet\" style=\"--fc:var(--nav)\">\n  <div class=\"deep-head\">\n    <div><div class=\"dk\">Deep dive · Competence 01</div><h2>The passage plan, stage by stage</h2></div>\n    <div class=\"dp\">Navigation<br>Page 01 / 01</div>\n  </div>\n  <p>Do not describe a passage plan as a list of waypoints. Describe it as a <b>decision process</b>: what you gathered, what you chose, what could go wrong, and how you would know.</p>\n  <div class=\"two-col\">\n    <div>\n      <h3>The five gates</h3>\n      <table>\n        <tr><th style=\"width:19%\">Stage</th><th>What you do</th><th>What you say</th></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Appraise</b></td><td>Charts, publications, weather, tide, load line, traffic, piracy, environmental limits, ship's condition.</td><td>“I start with the information pack and the risks — not the route.”</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Plan</b></td><td>Berth to berth: waypoints, courses, distances, UKC, turn radii, abort points, contingency anchorages.</td><td>“Every leg has a safe track, a limit and a way out.”</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Brief</b></td><td>Bridge team roles, pilot exchange, checklists, ECDIS settings, communications.</td><td>“The plan is only real when the bridge team can use it.”</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Execute</b></td><td>Departure, pilotage, coastal passage, ocean passage, arrival.</td><td>“I monitor against the plan, not from memory.”</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Monitor</b></td><td>Fixes, XTE, weather, traffic, ETA; change and record.</td><td>“If the facts change, the plan changes — and I record why.”</td></tr>\n      </table>\n      <h3>Route-check questions</h3>\n      <ul class=\"mini-list\">\n        <li>Is the chart the largest scale available and fully updated?</li>\n        <li>Is the safety contour deeper than my worst-case UKC?</li>\n        <li>Have I marked no-go areas, shoals, wrecks, cables and precautionary areas?</li>\n        <li>Are the turns achievable at the planned speed and radius?</li>\n        <li>Do I have an abort point and a contingency anchorage on every leg?</li>\n        <li>Have I briefed the bridge team and the pilot on the limits?</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <h3>UKC — say it like this</h3>\n      <div class=\"formula\">UKC = charted depth + height of tide − draught − squat − allowance</div>\n      <p>The allowance is where management judgement shows: chart accuracy (CATZOC), heel, swell, silting, dredging, tide prediction error, and company policy. State the number, then state the risk if it is wrong.</p>\n      <div class=\"note\"><b>Memory hook — “D-T-S-A”:</b> Depth + Tide − Ship − Squat − Allowance. If the answer is less than the company minimum, the route is not usable at that state of tide.</div>\n      <h3>What changes the plan?</h3>\n      <div class=\"taglist\">\n        <span class=\"tag\">weather</span><span class=\"tag\">traffic</span><span class=\"tag\">tide</span><span class=\"tag\">draught</span><span class=\"tag\">engine problem</span><span class=\"tag\">cargo shift</span><span class=\"tag\">pilot delay</span><span class=\"tag\">ice</span><span class=\"tag\">piracy</span><span class=\"tag\">visibility</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"say\"><b>If they ask “why this route?”</b><br>“It keeps me in the deepest water for the longest time, avoids the TSS crossing at the peak traffic period, and gives me two abort anchorages before the pilot station. The cost is 40 minutes, which I would rather spend than risk a UKC problem.”</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-top:13pt;\">\n  <h3>Plan the funnel, not just the line</h3>\n  <svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 92\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;margin:2pt 0 4pt 0;\">\n    <path d=\"M0 46 L500 8 L500 84 L0 46 Z\" fill=\"#f4f8f9\" stroke=\"#1f6f8b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n    <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"54\" stroke=\"#1f6f8b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n    <line x1=\"210\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#1f6f8b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n    <line x1=\"330\" y1=\"21\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"71\" stroke=\"#1f6f8b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n    <line x1=\"440\" y1=\"13\" x2=\"440\" y2=\"79\" stroke=\"#1f6f8b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n    <text x=\"14\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"8\" fill=\"#10263d\">OCEAN</text>\n    <text x=\"112\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"8\" fill=\"#10263d\">COASTAL</text>\n    <text x=\"222\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"8\" fill=\"#10263d\">PILOT STATION</text>\n    <text x=\"342\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"8\" fill=\"#10263d\">APPROACH</text>\n    <text x=\"452\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"8\" fill=\"#10263d\">BERTH</text>\n  </svg>\n  <p>As the funnel narrows, the options run out and the risk goes up. That is why the plan becomes more detailed — and the abort points closer together — as you approach the berth.</p>\n  </div></div>"
