    "deep": "\n<div class=\"deep sheet\" style=\"--fc:var(--nav)\">\n  <div class=\"deep-head\">\n    <div><div class=\"dk\">Deep dive · Competence 05</div><h2>COLREGs: the rules you will actually use</h2></div>\n    <div class=\"dp\">Navigation<br>Page 01 / 01</div>\n  </div>\n  <p>Do not recite all 38 rules. Learn the <b>situation → rule → action</b> pattern, then practise saying it in under 30 seconds.</p>\n  <table>\n    <tr><th style=\"width:10%\">Rule</th><th style=\"width:28%\">Situation</th><th>What you do</th><th style=\"width:18%\">Memory hook</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>5</b></td><td>Look-out</td><td>Keep a proper look-out by sight and hearing and by all available means; report what you see.</td><td>Eyes, ears, radar, AIS.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>6</b></td><td>Safe speed</td><td>Set speed for visibility, traffic, weather, sea room, draught, night background and stopping distance.</td><td>Stop in time.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>7</b></td><td>Risk of collision</td><td>Use all available means; if in doubt, assume risk exists. Watch the bearing, not just the range.</td><td>Doubt = risk.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>8</b></td><td>Action to avoid</td><td>Early, substantial, positive, with ample time; avoid small successive alterations; check the result.</td><td>Big, early, obvious.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>9</b></td><td>Narrow channel</td><td>Keep to the starboard edge; avoid crossing; do not anchor unless necessary.</td><td>Keep right.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>10</b></td><td>Traffic separation schemes</td><td>Use the lane, keep clear of the separation zone, cross at right angles, avoid anchoring.</td><td>Lane, not shortcut.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>13</b></td><td>Overtaking</td><td>The overtaking vessel keeps out of the way until finally past and clear.</td><td>Coming from aft = give way.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>14</b></td><td>Head-on</td><td>Both alter to starboard; pass port-to-port.</td><td>Red to red.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>15</b></td><td>Crossing</td><td>The vessel with the other on her starboard side gives way; avoid crossing ahead.</td><td>See red, give way.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>16</b></td><td>Give-way vessel</td><td>Take early and substantial action; do not wait for the stand-on vessel.</td><td>Act first.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>17</b></td><td>Stand-on vessel</td><td>Hold course and speed; may act if the give-way vessel is not taking action; do not alter to port for a crossing vessel.</td><td>Hold, then act.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>18</b></td><td>Responsibilities</td><td>Power-driven vessels give way to sail, fishing, constrained-by-draught and not-under-command vessels.</td><td>Least manoeuvrable wins.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>19</b></td><td>Restricted visibility</td><td>Safe speed, radar, sound signals, risk assessment; no stand-on/give-way rights in the same way.</td><td>Fog changes the game.</td></tr>\n  </table>\n  <div class=\"two-col\">\n    <div class=\"note\"><b>Rule 2 is not a licence.</b> You may depart from the rules only to avoid immediate danger, and you must still use good seamanship. Say what the danger was, what you did, and why.</div>\n    <div class=\"say\"><b>Crossing answer in one breath:</b> “I see a vessel on my starboard side, so I am the give-way vessel under Rule 15. I will make an early and substantial alteration to starboard, keep clear, check the bearing, and record the action.”</div>\n  </div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-top:12pt;\">\n  <h3>Lights and shapes you must recognise</h3>\n  <table class=\"compact\">\n    <tr><th style=\"width:24%\">Vessel</th><th>Day shape</th><th>Night lights</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Power-driven, underway</b></td><td>None</td><td>Masthead light(s), sidelights, sternlight.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Fishing vessel</b></td><td>Two cones, apex together (trawling)</td><td>Red over white (trawling); red over red (not trawling); green over white (pair trawling).</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Not under command</b></td><td>Two black balls</td><td>Two red all-round lights.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Restricted in ability to manoeuvre</b></td><td>Ball, diamond, ball</td><td>Red, white, red all-round.</td></tr>\n  </table>\n  \n</div>\n</div>\n"
