    "say": "I would set up the radar, cross-check it with visual and AIS, understand the ARPA limits, and keep an independent picture.",
    "deep": "\n<div class=\"deep sheet\" style=\"--fc:var(--nav)\">\n  <div class=\"deep-head\">\n    <div><div class=\"dk\">Deep dive · Competence 06</div><h2>Radar, ARPA and blind pilotage</h2></div>\n    <div class=\"dp\">Navigation<br>Page 01 / 01</div>\n  </div>\n  <p>The examiner wants to know that you can turn the equipment into a <b>decision</b> — and that you know when the picture is lying to you.</p>\n  <div class=\"two-col\">\n    <div>\n      <h3>Radar set-up — the five checks</h3>\n      <ul class=\"mini-list\">\n        <li><b>Performance:</b> warm up, tune, gain, sea and rain clutter; check the performance monitor if fitted.</li>\n        <li><b>Stabilisation:</b> north-up or course-up; check the heading marker and compass input.</li>\n        <li><b>Range and rings:</b> choose a range that shows the pilotage area and the next hazard.</li>\n        <li><b>VRM/EBL:</b> use a fixed object; check the range and bearing against the chart.</li>\n        <li><b>ARPA:</b> acquire early, check the vectors, use a trial manoeuvre, watch for target swap.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h3>ARPA limitations</h3>\n      <div class=\"taglist\">\n        <span class=\"tag\">small targets</span><span class=\"tag\">low reflectivity</span><span class=\"tag\">sea clutter</span><span class=\"tag\">rain clutter</span><span class=\"tag\">shadow sectors</span><span class=\"tag\">target swap</span><span class=\"tag\">tracking lag</span><span class=\"tag\">wrong vectors</span><span class=\"tag\">AIS overlay errors</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"note\"><b>Say it:</b> “ARPA is an aid, not a collision-avoidance decision. I still use visual bearings, the radar picture and the COLREGs.”</div>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <h3>Blind pilotage plan</h3>\n      <ul class=\"mini-list\">\n        <li><b>Track:</b> mark the planned track and the abort point on the chart and radar.</li>\n        <li><b>Team:</b> conning officer, helmsman, lookout, radar/plot, engine room, pilot.</li>\n        <li><b>Clearing bearings/ranges:</b> a bearing or range that keeps you in safe water.</li>\n        <li><b>Echo sounder:</b> set the shallow alarm and the trend; use it as a cross-check.</li>\n        <li><b>Comms:</b> standard phrases, closed-loop helm orders, ROTI and speed checks.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h3>Parallel indexing in one line</h3>\n      <p>Pick a fixed object, draw a line parallel to the planned track through it, and keep the object on the same index mark. If it moves off the line, you are off track — correct before the error grows.</p>\n      <div class=\"formula\">XTE = distance the index has moved × chart scale</div>\n      <div class=\"say\"><b>Blind pilotage answer:</b> “I would plan the track, set clearing bearings and ranges, put the echo sounder on the shallow alarm, brief every role, and agree the abort point before we enter.”</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-top:13pt;\">\n  <h3>CPA, TCPA and the trial manoeuvre</h3>\n  <div class=\"two-col\">\n    <div>\n      <p><b>CPA</b> is the closest predicted distance; <b>TCPA</b> is the time to that point. ARPA derives them from the target's relative track. If the bearing is steady and the range is falling, risk exists — whatever the CPA says.</p>\n      <div class=\"formula\">Relative track → CPA / TCPA → decision</div>\n      <p>The trial manoeuvre lets you test a course or speed change before you make it. Check the new CPA/TCPA, then make the alteration and monitor the target's response.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <h3>Blind pilotage brief — who does what</h3>\n      <table>\n        <tr><th style=\"width:32%\">Role</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Conning officer</b></td><td>Owns the track, the speed and the abort decision.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Helmsman</b></td><td>Steers the ordered course; reports the heading.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Lookout</b></td><td>Visual/audible warning; reports contacts and lights.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Radar/plot</b></td><td>Parallel index, ranges, bearings, contacts.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Engine room</b></td><td>Ready manoeuvres; confirms speed and response.</td></tr>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"note\"><b>Check the radar, not just the picture:</b> performance monitor, tune, gain, sea/rain clutter, heading marker, range rings and a known VRM/EBL. <b>ARPA limits:</b> small targets, target swap, tracking lag and clutter. Cross-check visually and apply the COLREGs.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n"
