    "say": "I would confirm the data, set the safety contour and UKC, run route check, and know my backup before I trust the route.",
    "deep": "\n<div class=\"deep sheet\" style=\"--fc:var(--nav)\">\n  <div class=\"deep-head\">\n    <div><div class=\"dk\">Deep dive · Competence 07</div><h2>ECDIS: settings, route check and failure</h2></div>\n    <div class=\"dp\">Navigation<br>Page 01 / 01</div>\n  </div>\n  <p>ECDIS questions are really about <b>control</b>: do you know what the system is displaying, what it is ignoring, and what you would do without it?</p>\n  <div class=\"two-col\">\n    <div>\n      <h3>Safety settings — what and why</h3>\n      <table>\n        <tr><th style=\"width:34%\">Setting</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Safety contour</b></td><td>The line that separates safe from unsafe water; must be deeper than the worst-case UKC.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Safety depth</b></td><td>Soundings at or below this depth are highlighted; set it for the passage's minimum UKC.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Shallow/deep contours</b></td><td>Shapes the colour bands; a wrong contour can hide a shoal or make deep water look shallow.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Look-ahead</b></td><td>Gives warning at the planned speed; too short and the alarm is useless.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><b>Safety frame</b></td><td>Defines the area around the ship that is checked; keep it realistic for the scale.</td></tr>\n      </table>\n      <h3>Route check</h3>\n      <ul class=\"mini-list\">\n        <li>Check the route against the safety contour and no-go areas.</li>\n        <li>Check every turn: radius, wheel-over, speed and cross-track limit.</li>\n        <li>Check the notes and the chart updates along the route.</li>\n        <li>Check the route in both directions if the return leg is planned.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <h3>Before you trust the display</h3>\n      <ul class=\"mini-list\">\n        <li>Position sensor, gyro, log and radar overlay are all alive and agreeing.</li>\n        <li>ENC is official, current and the correct scale.</li>\n        <li>Alarms are enabled and audible; the backup is ready.</li>\n        <li>The bridge team knows which display is the primary and which is the backup.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h3>Failure drill</h3>\n      <div class=\"say\"><b>If ECDIS fails:</b> “I would switch to the approved backup, fix by an independent means, reduce speed, inform the master and the bridge team, and record the time and action. I would not continue at full speed while I rebuild the picture.”</div>\n      <div class=\"note\"><b>ENC vs RNC:</b> an ENC is vector data (S-57) with selectable display and alarms; an RNC is a raster scan of a paper chart. The RNC looks familiar, but it does not give the same automatic warnings.</div>\n      <div class=\"taglist\">\n        <span class=\"tag\">S-57 data</span><span class=\"tag\">S-52 display</span><span class=\"tag\">S-63 permits</span><span class=\"tag\">CATZOC</span><span class=\"tag\">manual update</span><span class=\"tag\">track history</span><span class=\"tag\">playback</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-top:13pt;\">\n  <h3>The ECDIS workflow</h3>\n  <table>\n    <tr><th style=\"width:16%\">Stage</th><th>What you do</th><th style=\"width:30%\">What you check</th></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Data</b></td><td>Load the official ENC, apply updates, check the permit and the scale.</td><td>Edition, update status, CATZOC, licence.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Settings</b></td><td>Set safety contour, safety depth, shallow/deep contours, UKC and look-ahead.</td><td>Contour deeper than worst-case UKC.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Route</b></td><td>Build the route, run route check, inspect turns and no-go areas.</td><td>XTE, turn radius, wheel-over, notes.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Execute</b></td><td>Monitor position, XTE, alarms and sensors; fix by an independent means.</td><td>Position, gyro, log, radar overlay.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><b>Recover</b></td><td>If it fails, switch to the backup, reduce speed, inform the master and record.</td><td>Backup, independent fix, time and action.</td></tr>\n  </table>\n  <div class=\"two-col\">\n    <div class=\"note\"><b>Alarms you must not ignore:</b> position failure, gyro/log failure, safety contour, safety depth, off-track, approach to a hazard, route check, anchor watch, system/backup failure.</div>\n    <div class=\"say\"><b>Failure answer:</b> “I would not navigate from memory or from a frozen screen. I would go to the approved backup, fix independently, reduce speed, tell the master and record the time. Then I would decide whether the passage can continue.”</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n"
